<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gelimer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned 530–534</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gelimer was the last king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. In 530 he deposed his pro-Roman cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilderic">Hilderic</a>, giving Emperor Justinian a pretext for war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> defeated him at Ad Decimum and Tricamarum in 533, and after a winter besieged in the mountains he surrendered in 534. He was paraded in Belisarius' triumph at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a> and given estates in Galatia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gelimer.jpg" alt="Gelimer" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BCnze_50_Denari_-_Gelimer_-_K%C3%B6nig_der_Vandalen_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
